.TH KEV\-POLLER 1 "2026-10-29" "unheaded 86590d34" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
kev\-poller \- Keep the CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog current on this host (ADR\-055).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kev\-poller
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Keep the CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog current on this host (ADR\-055).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B report
print a threat\-register refresh entry from the stored catalog (see kev\-poller report \-\-help)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-interval \fISTRING\fR
time between pulls, 15m..24h (default 1h)
.TP
.B \-\-keep \fIDURATION\fR
delete snapshots older than this (the newest is always kept) (default 720h0m0s)
.TP
.B \-\-listen \fISTRING\fR
HTTP listen addresses, comma\-separated, overriding \-\-port; off loopback needs AUTH_ENABLED=true
.TP
.B \-\-node \fISTRING\fR
node identifier (default: hostname)
.TP
.B \-\-once
pull once, print a summary, exit (non\-zero on failure)
.TP
.B \-\-port \fIN\fR
HTTP port on loopback for /health, /ready, /metrics, /api/v1/kev (default 19120)
.TP
.B \-\-stack \fISTRING\fR
stack file (config/kev\-poller/stack.yaml): tag entries the Kingdom runs
.TP
.B \-\-state\-dir \fISTRING\fR
where latest.json, state.json and snapshots/ live (default /var/lib/unheaded/threat\-feeds/cisa\-kev)
.TP
.B \-\-timeout \fIDURATION\fR
per\-pull HTTP timeout (default 1m0s)
.TP
.B \-\-url \fISTRING\fR
catalog URL (https only) (default https://www.cisa.gov/sites/default/files/feeds/known_exploited_vulnerabilities.json)
.TP
.B \-\-wotan \fISTRING\fR
Wotan HTTP address; empty disables publishing (default localhost:18000)
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
